messages:
Ana: support hit a crash after we flipped to invokeEnvelope. Their parser expected top-level `tool_call` and arguments as an object. Need a tiny compatibility note + examples.
jamie: can you paste the failing payload?
Ana: pasted from ticket:
```json
{
  "invokeEnvelope": {
    "tool": "search",
    "arguments": "{\"q\":\"pricing api\"}"
  }
}
```
marco: classic double-encoded arguments. Plan: add a short H3 under /docs/guides/structured-output.md called "Compatibility adapters" with tiny python/ts snippets and a recommendation to validate via JSON Schema.
tasha: CI checklist: run docs build + link-checker before merge. ci-bot: noted.
jamie: python adapter suggestion:
```py
import json
def normalize(env):
    a = env.get('arguments')
    if isinstance(a, str):
        try:
            return json.loads(a)
        except Exception:
            return {}
    return a or {}
```
marco: TS equivalent I'll add in PR. I'll open a draft PR and include a one-line unit test for reviewers.
tasha: editorial: define and use one term ("invoke envelope"). Also call out not to use regex to extract JSON.
marco: draft PR 4999 opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4999 (draft). tagging eng-ml for guidance on parsing recommendations.
ajna: thanks all — I'll send the support workaround and close when PR merged. :white_check_mark:
